 "kit": "A Light Infantry levy of the free villages, sworn to no nation: a padded jack of undyed tan linen, worn under a sleeveless surcoat of undyed grey wool that covers his whole chest and belly from the collar down to just below the knees, front and back, split at the front below the belt so the legs can stride and held at the waist by a belt; padded sleeves and leather bracers; a plain rounded iron skullcap over a padded coif; a short grey wool shoulder cape; wrapped legs and soft boots; a long ash-wood spear with a leaf-shaped iron head; a small round wooden shield whose face is painted plain pale grey, with a thin iron rim and a boss. Plain, practical, worn; no colours but grey, tan, leather brown and iron.",
